    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="eyebrow" style="font-size:26px; text-transform:uppercase; color:var(--white); font-weight:800;">Our Vision</h2>
      <div class="vision-grid">
        <div class="how-copy">
          <p style="color: var(--white);">The vision of Botaki Ba Afrika is to establish an African-led Art Institute in every African country, where African artists can learn, develop, exchange
          and preserve African knowledge alongside contemporary ways of living, through the promotion of indigenous practices. The institutes will serve
          primarily as skills development centres and will promote economic transformation and freedom within disadvantaged black communities
          through art.</p>
          <p style="color: var(--white);">Botaki Ba Afrika approaches creativity as an ecosystem rather than an output. We understand that strong creative practices emerge when artists are supported by:</p>
          <ul style="list-style:none; padding:0; margin:0;">
            <li style="font-size:14px; color:var(--white); padding:4px 0;">• Thoughtful project management</li>
            <li style="font-size:14px; color:var(--white); padding:4px 0;">• Contextual programming and curation</li>
            <li style="font-size:14px; color:var(--white); padding:4px 0;">• Studio and production support</li>
            <li style="font-size:14px; color:var(--white); padding:4px 0;">• Fair remuneration and clear structures</li>
            <li style="font-size:14px; color:var(--white); padding:4px 0;">• Platforms for dialogue, visibility, and reflection</li>
          </ul>
          <p style="color: var(--white);">Our methodology is deeply informed by ethnographic thinking, process-led facilitation and relational care. Whether working with artists, institutions,
          corporates or communities, we prioritise contextual understanding, listening and co-creation.</p>
        </div>

